From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 21:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Build without loader lock sampling

enable_loader_lock_sampling is a plain gni value, not an argument; set it
false so no process starts a LoaderLockSampler thread (PLA-384).
Apply after the pinned CEF stock patches.

Class: feature
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-17-cef-trim.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 .../cpp/stack_sampling/loader_lock_sampling.gni    |    4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/services/tracing/public/cpp/stack_sampling/loader_lock_sampling.gni b/services/tracing/public/cpp/stack_sampling/loader_lock_sampling.gni
index 2e08f3166a..6341da71ff 100644
--- a/services/tracing/public/cpp/stack_sampling/loader_lock_sampling.gni
+++ b/services/tracing/public/cpp/stack_sampling/loader_lock_sampling.gni
@@ -2,4 +2,6 @@
 # Use of this source code is governed by a BSD-style license that can be
 # found in the LICENSE file.
 
-enable_loader_lock_sampling = is_win && target_cpu == "x64"
+# Off: an embedder that must fit several processes in a small address space
+# runs no sampling thread in each.
+enable_loader_lock_sampling = false
